"Summary of earlier turns: I made one tool call, search with query \"clock\" and path \"apps/canvas\". It returned many matches (the driver output was cut off after 20000 of 35909 characters). Nothing has been edited yet, and I have not tied the matches to the ticket.\n\nWhere \"clock\" shows up in apps/canvas/src:\n- api/client.ts, api/events.ts and api/readPlane.ts mention the clock only in comments. readPlane.ts says it uses the formatter's clock helpers and never `new Date`, per the ADR 35 lint rule.\n- desk/DeskAlertModal.tsx (lines about 373-402) has a `clock(label, value, delay)` helper. It renders `.dm-clock` elements and adds the `late` or `ontime` class only when both the time and a numeric delay are present. A delay above 0 gives \"late\". DeskAlertModal.test.tsx covers this behavior.\n- desk/DeskCasePane.tsx (around line 530) renders `.case-clock` and `.case-clock-value`. Its tests are at about lines 390-414.\n- desk/notesModel.ts (line 180) and desk/timelineModel.ts (line 159) each define a local `clock(minute)` that formats minutes as HH:MM.\n- desk/SwapBoard.tsx, SwapDonorCard.tsx and swapModel.ts pass a `clock: RenderContext` through to `formatInstant` from canvas-format.\n- i18n/messages.ts has the keys desk.modal.clocksFailed, ops.clocks, ops.clock.base, ops.clock.utc and desk.swap.tag.departs, in English, Spanish and French.\n- insights/desk/ImmersiveDesk.tsx has an exported `clocks(epochMs, zone)` that returns `{local, z}`. It refreshes every 15 seconds. Its test checks that the hub clock is read in the tenant's zone and Z in UTC.\n- launchpad/horizonModel.ts has `clockedRead`, `listsFollowClock` and a connection re-grading that follows the scrubbed clock. The last visible line of the output is about line 97 of that file, and the rest was cut off.\n\nNext step: reread the ticket, pick the file that matches it (likely one of the desk/ or insights/desk/ clock files), and open it with the file-reading tool."
